Error [E1102]: `greet` can't cross into a task because `fn()` isn't sendable
  --> tests/ui/task_detach_unsound.jet:6:22
    |
  6 |     t :: tasks.spawn(() => greet)
    |                      ^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: a closure may hold outside state, so it must be handed over with `take` before it crosses this boundary; tasks and channels move owned values between threads
 Fix: give the task plain owned data, or remove the shared-view field before spawning

Error [E1102]: this task returns `fn()`, which isn't sendable
  --> tests/ui/task_detach_unsound.jet:6:22
    |
  6 |     t :: tasks.spawn(() => greet)
    |                      ^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: a closure may hold outside state, so it must be handed over with `take` before it crosses this boundary; tasks and channels move owned values between threads
 Fix: give the task plain owned data, or remove the shared-view field before spawning

Error [E1103]: can't detach task `t` — it captured a value that can't cross a thread boundary
  --> tests/ui/task_detach_unsound.jet:7:7
    |
  7 |     t.detach()
    |       ^^^^^^
 Why: a detached task runs unsupervised; it must only hold values it owns cleanly
 Fix: fix the E1102 error at the spawn site first, then `.detach()` is safe
